[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/546243506","html_url":"https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/33393#issuecomment-546243506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/33393","id":546243506,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NjI0MzUwNg==","user":{"login":"pshurygin","id":25816676,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1ODE2Njc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25816676?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin","html_url":"https://github.com/pshurygin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pshurygin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-10-25T07:47:50Z","updated_at":"2019-10-25T07:57:01Z","body":"I agree that this is a very confusing change. The problem here is when using OnPush, how would the insertion point component know if some bindings were changed in the external template, and mark itself for check?\r\n\r\nI can see that angular material is facing the same issue and they workaround it by disabling OnPush, which is not really a great thing to do as far as i'm concerned. Our angular app is actually using OnPush on every component, but now it looks it would not be possible to follow this strategy anymore.\r\n\r\nThe previous behavior looks absolutely logical to me (check template when either insertion point or the origin view is checked).\r\n\r\nA